WEBVTT

00:00:00.690 --> 00:00:09.740
<i>The countless flowers,
enveloped in light…</i>

00:00:09.740 --> 00:00:19.840
<i>…gaze at tomorrow
with unwavering eyes.</i>

00:00:32.340 --> 00:00:39.350
<i>Everyone wishes for me to be pure…</i>

00:00:39.350 --> 00:00:46.810
<i>…but what can I bring
with me to the frayed skies?</i>

00:00:46.810 --> 00:00:53.900
<i>What I’ve made my own
by breaking off flowers in bloom…</i>

00:00:53.900 --> 00:00:59.530
<i>All such sinful things…</i>

00:00:59.530 --> 00:01:06.970
<i>Why did I stop making
promises with the future?</i>

00:01:06.970 --> 00:01:14.240
<i>Because even if I try
to run far from all the pain…</i>

00:01:14.240 --> 00:01:20.940
<i>…a cold wind rustles
my hair… Don’t you see?</i>

00:01:20.940 --> 00:01:27.900
<i>Where can I ever find the answer?</i>

00:02:15.820 --> 00:02:17.240
Just one.

00:02:17.240 --> 00:02:20.240
You just said,
“This will be easy,” didn’t you?

00:02:27.300 --> 00:02:28.680
That fool…

00:02:28.680 --> 00:02:32.420
The Simile Simoun
is a Simoun prototype…

00:02:32.880 --> 00:02:36.790
It hasn’t received
the grace of Tempus Spatium.

00:02:36.790 --> 00:02:39.630
It can’t draw a Ri Majon wake.

00:02:41.640 --> 00:02:47.640
<b>The Blue Spring</b>

00:02:54.430 --> 00:02:56.150
Such beautiful lines.

00:02:56.570 --> 00:02:59.900
Watch closely. Maju isn’t just practice.

00:03:00.400 --> 00:03:04.940
Because it’ll be your souls and
bodies that control the Simouns’ flight.

00:03:04.940 --> 00:03:08.430
Sibylla Elly, why are
you dressed like that?

00:03:11.950 --> 00:03:16.460
This is the last time I’ll ever
see anything as beautiful as this.

00:03:21.460 --> 00:03:24.970
That’s the emerald pattern…

00:03:28.310 --> 00:03:29.810
Impossible!

00:03:33.600 --> 00:03:34.940
What’s she thinking?

00:03:34.940 --> 00:03:36.270
She’s crazy!

00:03:41.510 --> 00:03:44.280
Does this look like a real Simoun?

00:03:56.530 --> 00:03:58.400
Where did you find her?

00:03:58.400 --> 00:03:59.380
She enlisted.

00:04:00.170 --> 00:04:03.830
Enlisted? That’s hard to believe.

00:04:04.390 --> 00:04:09.640
Who’d volunteer at a time like this,
knowing they’d have to go into battle?

00:04:27.460 --> 00:04:28.910
That’s…

00:04:55.420 --> 00:04:59.660
Are you in Tempest too?
Nobody else joined the battle.

00:04:59.660 --> 00:05:01.170
I was alone…

00:05:01.170 --> 00:05:02.320
What were you thinking?

00:05:02.320 --> 00:05:04.110
But I was alone…

00:05:04.110 --> 00:05:07.740
Simulating the Emerald
Ri Majon of all things.

00:05:07.740 --> 00:05:10.370
How would that make
Neviril feel if she saw it?

00:05:11.610 --> 00:05:13.580
Was I doing a Ri Majon?

00:05:15.080 --> 00:05:17.080
Who’s Neviril?

00:05:18.070 --> 00:05:21.590
When Simoun sibyllae take to the
skies, it’s called praying to the skies.

00:05:22.320 --> 00:05:25.800
Make sure you never
use the word battle again.

00:05:32.090 --> 00:05:33.390
So who’s Neviril?

00:05:33.390 --> 00:05:36.800
Neviril is the regina of Chor Tempest.

00:05:36.800 --> 00:05:41.970
Sibylla Aurea, the Golden Priestess!
I want to pair up with her!

00:05:41.970 --> 00:05:42.900
No way…

00:05:43.510 --> 00:05:46.650
Why not?
She’s the top Simoun rider, right?

00:05:46.650 --> 00:05:48.660
Simoun rider…

00:05:48.660 --> 00:05:50.660
Yeah, till now.

00:05:50.660 --> 00:05:52.660
But it might not be true anymore.

00:05:54.160 --> 00:05:58.430
Because you’re amazing!
I think I really like you.

00:05:58.430 --> 00:06:00.670
Hey, why don’t you pair up with me?

00:06:01.430 --> 00:06:03.670
Listen, where’s this Neviril?

00:06:36.920 --> 00:06:40.530
It brings back memories.
When we were trainees…

00:06:40.530 --> 00:06:44.420
…nothing made me happier
than waiting on you.

00:06:44.830 --> 00:06:46.880
That hasn’t changed one bit.

00:06:47.430 --> 00:06:50.430
Dressed like that…
you’re leaving the ship too?

00:06:50.430 --> 00:06:55.310
Yes. Since it’s been a long
time since my 17th birthday…

00:06:55.310 --> 00:06:59.890
I’ve decided to go to the Spring.
And I have one last favor to ask…

00:07:00.550 --> 00:07:01.650
What is it?

00:07:03.980 --> 00:07:05.610
I’m afraid…

00:07:07.220 --> 00:07:09.890
…of going to the Spring.

00:07:09.890 --> 00:07:12.160
If you don’t mind…

00:07:16.230 --> 00:07:20.580
Of course, Elly.
I will accompany you.

00:07:20.580 --> 00:07:24.590
Neviril! Anyone seen Neviril?

00:07:25.440 --> 00:07:27.210
Have you seen Neviril?

00:07:27.210 --> 00:07:30.330
Stop calling her that. Please…

00:07:30.840 --> 00:07:32.910
…um, Aer.

00:07:32.910 --> 00:07:36.690
This is Chor Tempest’s
maintenance hangar.

00:07:36.690 --> 00:07:38.600
Where’s Neviril?

00:07:39.650 --> 00:07:41.250
You here, Neviril?

00:07:41.250 --> 00:07:44.990
This is the cafeteria.
And this is the ballroom.

00:07:44.990 --> 00:07:46.610
Where’s Neviril?

00:07:54.160 --> 00:07:55.400
Wow!

00:07:55.400 --> 00:07:57.620
This is the forward deck.

00:07:58.130 --> 00:08:01.150
Neviril, what’s the meaning of this?

00:08:01.150 --> 00:08:03.510
Elly said she’s going to the Spring.

00:08:03.510 --> 00:08:07.820
She’s unpaired at the moment,
so I’m accompanying her.

00:08:07.820 --> 00:08:11.380
You’re lying.
Then why are you taking luggage?

00:08:11.810 --> 00:08:15.230
I haven’t made up my mind yet.

00:08:15.230 --> 00:08:21.850
So there’s a chance that
I might enter the Spring as well.

00:08:22.360 --> 00:08:23.410
If so…

00:08:23.410 --> 00:08:25.350
But you can’t…

00:08:25.350 --> 00:08:28.900
You can’t do that!
Because if you enter the Spring…

00:08:28.900 --> 00:08:33.310
…that means you’ll have Tempus
Spatium choose your gender, right?

00:08:33.310 --> 00:08:34.910
It’s none of your business.

00:08:35.880 --> 00:08:36.990
Who are you?

00:08:36.990 --> 00:08:41.220
Aer. Chor Tempest Simoun sibylla.

00:08:41.220 --> 00:08:44.210
I’d like to pair up with you.

00:08:44.210 --> 00:08:48.250
Those who are neither male
nor female can fly Simouns.

00:08:48.250 --> 00:08:50.290
Now’s our only chance.

00:08:50.290 --> 00:08:54.220
Yet if you go to the Spring,
you can’t be my pair.

00:08:55.590 --> 00:08:57.260
She couldn’t to begin with.

00:08:57.760 --> 00:09:02.780
My 17th birthday
passed over a year ago.

00:09:02.780 --> 00:09:05.390
You’re an exceptional Simoun sibylla…

00:09:05.850 --> 00:09:10.610
…and in this state of emergency,
the nation can’t afford to lose you.

00:09:10.610 --> 00:09:14.450
So Onasia has agreed not
to summon you to the Spring…

00:09:14.450 --> 00:09:16.110
Please, Paraietta.

00:09:16.680 --> 00:09:18.370
Let me go.

00:09:21.480 --> 00:09:23.040
Please.

00:09:29.040 --> 00:09:32.570
We are all born as females.

00:09:32.570 --> 00:09:38.550
But to create a society,
half the population must be male.

00:09:38.550 --> 00:09:43.040
Tempus Spatium has decreed
the world should be so.

00:09:43.040 --> 00:09:48.940
Once we’ve turned 17, we’re allowed
to choose our permanent gender.

00:09:49.510 --> 00:09:54.260
But in the case of Simoun sibyllae,
this can be delayed.

00:09:54.260 --> 00:09:59.160
Our nation, Kyuukoku, has gotten
invaded by countless countries.

00:09:59.660 --> 00:10:02.160
Our only hope of battling
them are Simouns…

00:10:02.930 --> 00:10:07.160
…and you sibyllae,
who can talk with the Simouns.

00:10:07.160 --> 00:10:12.110
If you wish, you may delay
your pilgrimage to the Spring.

00:10:12.110 --> 00:10:17.510
If, on the other hand, you yearn for
the Spring, we cannot stop you.

00:10:18.440 --> 00:10:20.220
Especially Chor Tempest…

00:10:20.220 --> 00:10:26.020
Since the war began, you and Chor
Caput have suffered great losses.

00:10:26.820 --> 00:10:31.520
Those who’ve turned 17 are free
to choose the same path as Neviril.

00:10:31.990 --> 00:10:33.520
There’s no way I would.

00:10:33.970 --> 00:10:38.400
Man or woman, I haven’t
decided yet. I don’t even want to.

00:10:38.400 --> 00:10:42.450
As long as I’m in battle with a Simoun,
I won’t have to go to the Spring.

00:10:42.880 --> 00:10:46.450
That’s why I came here.
Are you guys different?

00:10:46.450 --> 00:10:50.910
No question.
Once you’re of age, you have to go.

00:10:50.910 --> 00:10:54.110
It means you’re going
to become an adult.

00:10:54.110 --> 00:10:58.470
But right now, the nation
needs our powers, so…

00:10:58.470 --> 00:11:00.890
Oh? Is that right?

00:11:00.890 --> 00:11:05.470
Then you’ve all already decided
to become a man or woman?

00:11:07.520 --> 00:11:09.290
Have you, Big Sister?

00:11:30.080 --> 00:11:31.120
Listen, you…

00:11:31.720 --> 00:11:33.630
It’s fine, Elly.

00:11:33.630 --> 00:11:37.360
One last time…
Won’t you pair up with me?

00:11:37.360 --> 00:11:41.130
I want you to see me fly as
an auriga to the great temple below.

00:11:45.090 --> 00:11:47.140
Then I’ll have them
get a Simoun ready!

00:11:55.200 --> 00:11:57.680
Well? How’s my driving?

00:11:57.680 --> 00:12:00.450
Not “driving,”
“speaking with the Simoun.”

00:12:00.450 --> 00:12:02.650
Oh, sorry. I’m just so psyched.

00:12:03.220 --> 00:12:06.660
Because this is the first time
I’ve touched a real Simoun.

00:12:06.660 --> 00:12:08.450
First time?

00:12:10.950 --> 00:12:13.320
I’ve always wanted to ride one.

00:12:13.320 --> 00:12:14.660
Really?

00:12:14.660 --> 00:12:17.300
You know what I mean, don’t you?

00:12:17.300 --> 00:12:19.460
Everything has changed.

00:12:19.970 --> 00:12:24.210
Because you’re not “praying to
the skies” for Tempus Spatium…

00:12:24.210 --> 00:12:26.470
…but for war?

00:12:26.470 --> 00:12:27.720
Yes.

00:12:28.210 --> 00:12:29.840
There’s no difference.

00:12:29.840 --> 00:12:32.480
You don’t understand.

00:12:34.440 --> 00:12:37.940
What kind…
What kind of place the battlefield is.

00:12:40.550 --> 00:12:45.510
I do. Because I trained
on the front lines in the south.

00:12:46.960 --> 00:12:52.440
Before the war, sibyllae would go to
the Spring when they turned 17, right?

00:12:52.440 --> 00:12:53.460
Yes.

00:12:53.460 --> 00:12:59.960
But now, the great temple’s laws
say we don’t have to go to the Spring.

00:13:00.700 --> 00:13:02.210
As long as we’re winning this war…

00:13:11.810 --> 00:13:13.640
Thank you, Aer.

00:13:20.160 --> 00:13:22.900
How rude. She’s an auriga, right?

00:13:22.900 --> 00:13:24.060
Yes.

00:13:24.060 --> 00:13:28.950
So she made you fly as her sagitta?
The finest auriga in the nation?

00:13:39.960 --> 00:13:45.970
Out of all of us here, is Paraietta
the only one who’s turned 17?

00:13:47.250 --> 00:13:49.970
Big Sister, you’ll be
17 next month, right?

00:13:53.970 --> 00:13:57.480
Either way, we all will be soon.

00:13:57.960 --> 00:14:02.700
Aren’t you going after Neviril?
You’re going to become a man for her…

00:14:02.700 --> 00:14:05.240
You made
that decision long ago, right?

00:14:06.250 --> 00:14:10.700
I still feel that there are things
I need to accomplish here.

00:14:48.540 --> 00:14:50.910
Elly, have you decided?

00:14:52.180 --> 00:14:54.870
Which gender you’ll
choose at the Spring.

00:14:58.320 --> 00:15:00.870
Um, no.

00:15:01.540 --> 00:15:02.630
I see.

00:15:02.630 --> 00:15:07.810
I’ve always been female, so I think
it’d be more natural to stay one.

00:15:07.810 --> 00:15:10.780
I might also want to become a male.

00:15:10.780 --> 00:15:15.530
After all, there aren’t a lot of job
opportunities unless you’re a man.

00:15:20.440 --> 00:15:23.900
I know you must be weary,
Simoun sibylla, but…

00:15:25.180 --> 00:15:26.480
I don’t mind.

00:15:28.480 --> 00:15:33.130
Simoun sibylla…
Such a beautiful sight…

00:15:33.130 --> 00:15:37.900
O priestess, please guide
our nation to the righteous path.

00:15:37.900 --> 00:15:39.900
Please protect us.

00:15:52.010 --> 00:15:53.820
Are you Neviril?

00:15:53.820 --> 00:15:55.140
Yes.

00:16:02.280 --> 00:16:04.900
If I’m with you,
I think I’ll have fun flying.

00:16:47.060 --> 00:16:49.140
O sibyllae…

00:16:49.140 --> 00:16:54.600
We are overjoyed to know that
your time for prayer is now over.

00:16:55.500 --> 00:17:00.770
We thank you for having
protected us all thus far…

00:17:38.150 --> 00:17:40.220
What should I do?

00:17:40.220 --> 00:17:43.860
I’m supposed to think
“male” or “female” in my head…

00:17:43.860 --> 00:17:47.450
…but what happens if I think of both?

00:17:47.860 --> 00:17:51.210
You’ll be fine.
There’s nothing to worry about, Elly.

00:17:54.200 --> 00:17:55.760
Onasia…

00:18:01.440 --> 00:18:03.740
Great Priestess Onasia…

00:18:04.740 --> 00:18:10.770
Forgive me for not journeying here
though my 17th birthday is long past.

00:18:11.350 --> 00:18:15.150
Sibylla Elly, enter the Spring.

00:18:15.150 --> 00:18:17.780
And offer a prayer…

00:19:00.030 --> 00:19:01.330
No…

00:19:01.800 --> 00:19:04.990
What should I do? I can’t decide!

00:19:22.280 --> 00:19:28.420
The holy sounds of Tempus Spatium
have just been bestowed upon you.

00:19:42.840 --> 00:19:47.210
I was told that starting
today, my name is Eliph.

00:19:48.110 --> 00:19:49.200
Yes.

00:19:50.180 --> 00:19:52.040
Congratulations.

00:19:52.810 --> 00:19:55.490
They say your voice
changes overtime…

00:19:55.490 --> 00:19:59.580
…and your chest gets smaller, but…

00:20:00.420 --> 00:20:04.590
Nothing’s really changed, has it?

00:20:05.160 --> 00:20:06.570
Right.

00:20:06.570 --> 00:20:10.050
Nothing has changed, Eliph.

00:20:43.630 --> 00:20:46.150
Well, Sibylla Roatreamon.

00:20:46.150 --> 00:20:48.600
You’re staying too, my lady?

00:20:48.600 --> 00:20:53.680
I grew up being told
I should become a sibylla…

00:20:53.680 --> 00:20:55.980
…so if I went home now,
they’d yell at me.

00:20:56.490 --> 00:21:00.440
We all have one, don’t we? A reason…

00:21:15.630 --> 00:21:18.750
The thing is…
I can’t fly this alone, right?

00:21:50.030 --> 00:21:52.270
You didn’t go to the Spring?

00:21:52.270 --> 00:21:56.100
I did go. But I decided not to enter.

00:22:06.680 --> 00:22:08.050
Higher.

00:22:09.050 --> 00:22:10.890
Than our ship?

00:22:11.420 --> 00:22:12.910
Higher.

00:22:13.390 --> 00:22:14.640
Please.

00:22:41.120 --> 00:22:47.830
<i>It is played by my wounds…
the song of prayer.</i>

00:22:47.830 --> 00:22:52.070
<i>Let it ring out over
the grieving universe.</i>

00:22:52.070 --> 00:22:59.140
<i>Can we change tomorrow?
Don’t be afraid.</i>

00:22:59.140 --> 00:23:06.970
<i>I want to let you know
how my heart’s overflowing.</i>

00:23:15.550 --> 00:23:19.620
<i>“I want to get closer to you.”
“I want to feel your pulse.”</i>

00:23:19.620 --> 00:23:24.760
<i>I was too defiant,
and I took the long way around.</i>

00:23:24.760 --> 00:23:28.810
<i>The blue moon is swaying silently.</i>

00:23:28.810 --> 00:23:32.810
<i>My true heart’s desire is you.</i>

00:23:32.810 --> 00:23:38.400
<i>I can’t reach you.
My tears of pain trickle down.</i>

00:23:38.710 --> 00:23:44.230
<i>Soar away into the sky, song of prayer.</i>

00:23:44.230 --> 00:23:47.660
<i>Carrying my love that came too late.</i>

00:23:47.660 --> 00:23:53.330
<i>What can I do to change tomorrow?</i>

00:23:53.330 --> 00:23:59.730
<i>Just hold on to “now” the way it is…</i>

00:24:04.920 --> 00:24:06.590
<b>To Be Continued</b>

00:24:07.570 --> 00:24:11.550
Shoukoku’s massive long-range cannons are
headed this way.

00:24:14.610 --> 00:24:16.850
Next time on Simoun…

00:24:15.470 --> 00:24:19.970
<b>The Distant War</b>

00:24:16.850 --> 00:24:18.720
The Distant War.
